    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The author would like to thank Professor B. Gramsch for drawing the author’s attention to the b-calculus, Professor B. A. Plamenevskij for suggesting the problem of describing the Jacobson topology of the algebra B(Z,bΩ12), and Professor A. Yu. Kokotov for raising the question what the length of B(Z,bΩ12) is at the Spring School Operator algebras with symbolic structure on singular manifolds, index theory, and asymptotics at Potsdam (February, 98)."
